dialogue vane
  node root vane "Clerks don't steer. Say your piece and get off my deck."
    > "About your three terms." if vane_terms -> count
    > "Your course is the long way round." if looked:marrow_cabin.chart and not vane_terms -> course
    > "What happened to the other ships?" -> ships
    > "Where's your navigator?" if not seen:vane.pell -> pell
    > "Nothing, captain." -> bye
  node pell vane "Pell. Forty years at sea. Died last winter, mid-sentence. I'd give a lot to know how it ended."
    > "What happened to the other ships?" -> ships
    > "I'm sorry." -> bye
  node course vane "We sail Pell's line, north of the reef. Two days longer. Nobody's ever been lost on it. The south side kills anyone who tries."
    > "What if there's a way through?" -> through
    > "Understood, captain." -> bye
  node through vane "Then show me on the chart. Something better than hope. I've a hold full of hope and it pays badly."
    > "Yes, captain." -> bye
  node ships vane "Six ships in three years. Five found drifting, holds empty, no crew. The first was the Arcadia. Nobody found a plank of her."
    -> insurers
  node insurers vane "The insurers paid on all six. Weather. That year they refused my claim for a real storm."
    -> funny
  node funny vane "Funny thing, weather."
    > "Who are you carrying for now?" if not seen:vane.cray -> cray
    > "Where's your navigator?" if not seen:vane.pell -> pell
    > "I'll let you get on." -> bye
  node cray vane "Cray's charter. Cray's crates. Cray's money. It's the only work left. …It pays for the stew. Some of us eat."
    > "Where's your navigator?" if not seen:vane.pell -> pell
    > "I'll let you get on." -> bye
  node count vane "A navigator, a crew, and a reason Pell would have. Count them for me. Slowly."
    > "Quill has sworn to the line." if quill_navigator -> quill
    > "The crew will sail it." if crew_agree -> crew
    > "Still counting." -> counting
  node quill vane "Quill. Best eyes Pell ever saw, worst patience. He'd have liked this. He'd have pretended not to."
    > "The crew will sail it." if crew_agree -> crew
    > "That's one." -> counting
  node crew vane "Hobb told me. He rolled up his sleeve to do it. Nine years, and I'd never seen his whole arm."
    > "That's two." -> counting
  node counting vane "And a reason Pell would have. He never said a word he hadn't written down first. Off you go."
  node bye vane "Off my deck, clerk."
  # The compass on the chart (rooms.ts) opens here.
  node compass vane "Through the reef. There is no way through the reef, clerk. That's what a reef is."
    > "My father found one." -> father
  node father vane "And who was your father, to find holes in reefs?"
    > "Ansel Fenn. Of the Arcadia." -> ansel
  node ansel vane "Ansel Fenn ran the Straits faster than anyone. He never said how. The old men in the Keel talk about the Needle, a gap in the reef."
    -> ansel2
  node ansel2 vane "I took it for a story for selling drinks. …So. That's how."
    -> needle
  node needle narrator "She looks at the needle for a long moment. The needle looks back."
    -> no
  node no vane "No. A dead man's compass and a clerk's word. I buried one navigator. I won't drown another."
    > "Then what would it take?" -> terms
      set vane_terms
    > "I could fill in a form." -> form
      set vane_terms
    > "He isn't dead, captain. He's overdue." -> overdue
  node overdue vane "…Spoken like a man who's never written the other word."
    > "Then what would it take?" -> terms
      set vane_terms
    > "I could fill in a form." -> form
      set vane_terms
  node form vane "If a form could get a ship through that reef, Cray would own the reef. …No. Here's what it takes."
    -> terms
  node terms vane "Three things. A navigator who'll swear to the line. A crew who'll sail it."
    -> terms2
  node terms2 vane "And a reason Pell would have. He never dared the south side. Give me one."
    note vane_terms "Vane will run the reef on three terms: a navigator to swear to the line, a crew to sail it, and a reason Pell would have had."
    > "Yes, captain." -> END
    > "Three things. I've done harder lists before breakfast." -> lists
  node lists vane "It's past breakfast. Go and eat. Dorrit's been sulking at the stew all morning."
  # Pell's log, given once the other two terms are met (rooms.ts, marrow_cabin).
  node log fenn "Pell's last entry. It doesn't finish."
    -> there
  node there vane "I know. I was there."
    > "You said you'd give a lot to know the ending." if seen:vane.pell -> read
    > "May I read it to you?" -> read
  node read fenn "“If Ansel's boy ever comes aboard with the old man's compass, tell the captain she should…”"
    -> boy
  node boy narrator "Ansel's boy. Nobody has called me that in three years. I read it as written. My voice breaks once."
    -> silence
  node silence narrator "Vane is quiet for a long time. The timbers start talking to fill the gap."
    -> trust
  node trust vane "Trust the boy. That's how it ends. Pell and Ansel drank rum together every winter. Of course Ansel told him."
    -> trust2
  node trust2 vane "And Pell never told me, because I never trusted anyone."
    -> hat
  node hat narrator "She stands and puts on her hat. I gather that's serious."
    -> coward
  node coward vane "Fine. Forty years, and you finally give an order. You make me finish it for you."
    -> orders
  node orders vane "Get to the bow, clerk. Quill takes the wheel. You call the bearings. And if you're wrong, call them louder."
    > "Aye, captain." -> END
      take pell_log
      set vane_convinced
    > "I've never said “aye” before." -> aye
      take pell_log
      set vane_convinced
  node aye vane "You'll get the hang of it. Most people do by the second reef."
